            <ArticleTitle>Acute left main occlusion during transcatheter aortic valve implantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>653-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5603/KP.2013.0138</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a 92 year-old female with severe aortic stenosis who underwent TAVI. The procedure resulted with acute left main coronary artery occlusion requiring an immediate percutaneous coronary intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
